---
import { base } from '../../lib/base';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FlowHero from '../../components/FlowHero.astro';
import OldFlow from '../../components/OldFlow.astro';
import FiveWays from '../../components/FiveWays.astro';
import PasswordGate from '../../components/PasswordGate.astro';
import { site, projects } from '../../data/site';
import Check from '@lucide/astro/icons/check';

const project = projects.find((p) => p.slug === 'evertune')!;
---

<Layout title={`${project.title} · ${site.name}`} description={project.summary}>
	<div id="gated" class="gated">
	<article class="container study">
		<a class="back" href={`${base}/#work`}>← All case studies</a>

		<ul class="tags">
			{project.tags.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
		</ul>
		<h1>{project.title}</h1>

		<section>
			<h2>Overview</h2>
			<p>
				Evertune customers have more than one way to create the prompts that measure their AI visibility.
				They can start from a standard template, or use Evertune’s agent to create prompts based on how
				people actually prompt LLMs.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Context</h2>
			<p>
				At first, there was only one way to create prompts: the standard template. As Evertune grew, customer
				feedback showed that people wanted to run their own sets of prompts, so a new type of analysis was
				added.
			</p>
			<p>
				Before long, there were five different ways to create prompts. Each was added to meet a specific
				customer need, but over time the prompt creation experience became unwieldy and hard to use.
			</p>
			<p>
				Very soon, new users started saying that the prompt creation flow took too much time and was hard to
				use.
			</p>
			<FiveWays />
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>The problem</h2>
			<p>
				Getting to a set of prompts took many steps, and customers, especially new users, struggled to pick the
				right type of tracker. There were five main types, and one of them had three steps of its own. It was
				confusing before anyone had created a single prompt.
			</p>
			<OldFlow />
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>The insight</h2>
			<p>
				After collecting user feedback and analyzing how customers use the platform, it became clear that:
			</p>
			<ol class="points">
				<li><span class="n">1</span><span>Users primarily preferred Evertune’s suggested prompts.</span></li>
				<li>
					<span class="n">2</span><span
						>Pitch Report was only available to agencies, and it was essentially Suggested Prompts with a prompt limit.</span
					>
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="n">3</span><span>Only 10–15% of users had access to Product Category Analysis and Word Association.</span>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>The new experience</h2>
			<p>
				I wanted the design to align with Evertune’s long-term vision of an agentic platform experience.
				After learning more about the tools our customers already used, a chat-to-canvas flow felt like a
				natural fit.
			</p>
			<p>
				With the new agent experience, there is nothing to choose up front. Users begin prompt creation
				in a simple chat, use Evertune’s agent to modify the topics and prompts, and adjust the settings
				before running.
			</p>
			<div class="bleed">
				<FlowHero video={project.flow!} />
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>The impact</h2>
			<p class="pull">
				New customers find it much easier and more intuitive to create trackers and run prompts.
			</p>
			<ul class="wins">
				<li><Check size={20} strokeWidth={1.75} aria-hidden="true" />No onboarding steps needed</li>
				<li>
					<Check size={20} strokeWidth={1.75} aria-hidden="true" />No white-glove service from our customer success team
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</article>
	</div>

	<PasswordGate mode="immediate" />
</Layout>

<style>
	.study {
		max-width: 900px;
		padding-top: 140px;
		padding-bottom: 40px;
	}
	.back {
		display: inline-block;
		color: var(--muted);
		text-decoration: none;
		margin-bottom: 28px;
	}
	.back:hover {
		color: var(--accent);
	}
	h1 {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-weight: 400;
		font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
		line-height: 1.1;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		margin: 16px 0 12px;
	}
	section {
		margin-top: 56px;
	}
	section p {
		max-width: 62ch;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: var(--fg);
	}
	.tags {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 8px;
	}
	.tags li {
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		border: 1px solid #e3e3e3;
		border-radius: 999px;
		padding: 2px 10px;
	}
	/* The new-experience hero breaks out of the text column so the screens read larger */
	.bleed {
		position: relative;
		left: 50%;
		/* As wide as the page allows, but never taller than the room below the floating nav
		   (about 110px) once the step buttons are counted: the video is 1440:862, so its
		   height follows its width. */
		width: min(1400px, calc(100vw - 48px), max(560px, calc((100vh - 300px) * 1.6705 + 66px)));
		width: min(1400px, calc(100vw - 48px), max(560px, calc((100svh - 300px) * 1.6705 + 66px)));
		transform: translateX(-50%);
	}
	.bleed :global(.panel) {
		padding: clamp(14px, 2.4vw, 32px);
	}
	@media (max-width: 960px) {
		.bleed {
			left: 0;
			width: 100%;
			transform: none;
		}
	}
	.points {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 24px 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 16px;
		max-width: 62ch;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}
	.points li {
		display: flex;
		align-items: flex-start;
		gap: 14px;
	}
	.points .n {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		display: grid;
		place-items: center;
		width: 28px;
		height: 28px;
		margin-top: 1px;
		border-radius: 8px;
		background: #efefef;
		color: #555;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 500;
	}
	section p.pull {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.4vw, 2.3rem);
		line-height: 1.25;
		max-width: 28ch;
		margin: 0 0 24px;
	}
	.wins {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 12px;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}
	.wins li {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 12px;
	}
	.wins :global(svg) {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		padding: 5px;
		box-sizing: content-box;
		width: 20px;
		height: 20px;
		border-radius: 8px;
		background: #efefef;
		color: #555;
	}
</style>
